<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GFSA's Black Mountain Q1 net falls.</title>
<headline>GFSA's Black Mountain Q1 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending 13.21 vs 18.47</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  1.14 vs  2.64</p>
<p>    Sales					64.39 vs 91.59</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			  390,000 vs 367,000</p>
<p>Metal in concentrates produced (tonnes unless stated):</p>
<p>    - copper				   1,342 vs  1,173</p>
<p>    - lead				    20,831 vs 20,937</p>
<p>    - silver (kg)			   22,789 vs 24,291</p>
<p>    - zinc				     7,347 vs  7,289</p>
<p>Metal in concentrates sold (tonnes unless stated):</p>
<p>    - copper				   1,472 vs  2,630</p>
<p>    - lead				    16,186 vs 19,929</p>
<p>    - silver (kg)			   17,897 vs 27,843</p>
<p>    - zinc				     6,315 vs  8,164</p>
<p>Full name: Black Mountain Mineral Development Co (Pty) Ltd, managed by Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
